B.abh=new A.i(1321,"caution","THE SIGNS THAT SAY IT IS ALREADY SEPSIS - lethargy, feeding poorly, fever, irritability: systemic features like these point to sepsis, and to a worse outlook. A newborn who has gone quiet and stopped feeding is the emergency, whatever the umbilicus looks like.")
B.abw=new A.i(1321,"caution","THE SURGICAL EMERGENCY INSIDE THE MEDICAL ONE - where redness of the abdominal wall is spreading fast, or there is gas in the tissue around it, think necrotizing fasciitis and get a surgical opinion acutely. Suspect it too where intravenous antibiotics have produced no clinical improvement in 24 to 48 hours. The stakes are these: mortality of 60% to 85% has been reported where omphalitis is complicated by necrotizing fasciitis.")
