B.ab6=new A.i(1630,"caution","AN ASYMMETRICAL TONSIL IS A DIFFERENT REFERRAL ENTIRELY - asymmetry of the tonsils is itself an indication for surgery, to exclude cancer. In the palatine tonsils the cancers seen most are squamous cell carcinoma and lymphoma, and in a child almost all of them are lymphoma. One tonsil much bigger than the other, especially with neck nodes or weight loss, is urgent and does not wait for any episode count.")
B.a6E=new A.i(1630,"caution","THE COMPLICATIONS THAT MEAN SEND TODAY - a peritonsillar abscess, a retropharyngeal abscess, Lemierre syndrome, or a threatened airway all need escalating urgently. A quinsy has a recognisable face: sore throat on one side, trismus, the uvula pushed across, and a thick muffled voice, as though the child were speaking round a hot potato.")
