B.a7Z=new A.i(1768,"caution","RED FLAG - THE ALARMING FEATURES the article lists are loss of hearing or of vision at any age; tone that stays too low or too high; movements that are not symmetrical; no communicative speech by 16 months; a head circumference out of proportion; and the loss of skills the child had already gained. A child who spoke words and has stopped is a different and more urgent problem from one who never started.")
