B.aas=new A.i(1785,"caution","RED FLAG - Emergency ophthalmology referral is indicated when the haemorrhage follows trauma with suspected intraocular or retinal injury. Recurrence, bilateral involvement, systemic bruising, or anticoagulant therapy warrant further evaluation, and blood pressure measurement is essential in spontaneous or recurrent haemorrhage.")
