B.aa8=new A.i(1909,"caution","RED FLAG - OMPHALITIS: infection of the umbilicus and the tissue around it, seen most often in newborns, and classed as a medical emergency because it can run on quickly to systemic infection, to sepsis, and to death. Do not cauterise an infected umbilicus - admit it.")
