B.a5J=new A.i(777,"band:1:1 month to 12 years","50 to 180 mg/kg/day IV divided every 4 to 6 hours. Maximum 180 mg/kg/day under 50 kg; doses up to 300 mg/kg/day (maximum 12 g/day) have been used off-label in meningitis. From the twelfth birthday the formulary sends the reader to the adult dose, which is not on this card - it is for infants under three months.")
B.a7I=new A.i(1301,"band:0:4 to 12 years","One spray per nostril once daily, preferably in the morning - 27.5 mcg fluticasone furoate (maximum 55 mcg a day), or 50 mcg fluticasone propionate per spray (maximum 100 mcg a day). Some cases need twice daily, to a maximum of two sprays per nostril.")
B.a9H=new A.i(1318,"band:1:1 month and over","25 to 50 mg/kg, maximum 2 g, every 6 hours by intravenous infusion over 60 minutes - MSF's figure for a child of 1 month and over. Dilute each dose in 5 mL/kg of 0.9% sodium chloride or 5% glucose under 20 kg, and in a 100 mL bag at 20 kg and over.")
