B.aEx=new A.l("acne-vulgaris","Doxycycline","No sourced child acne regimen here; avoid doxycycline under 8 years.","oral.solid",'NICE Guideline NG198 Acne vulgaris: management, "Terms used in this guideline", entry "Oral lymecycline or oral doxycycline": "Formulation of either: 408 mg lymecycline daily / 100 mg doxycycline daily." The UK eMC Doxycycline 100mg Capsules SmPC section 4.2 states a lower figure for the same indication - "50 mg daily with food or fluid for 6 to 12 weeks" - and the DailyMed doxycycline capsule label states no acne dose at all, only that in severe acne doxycycline "may be useful adjunctive therapy". Under the tier list in docs/SOURCES.md a tier-1 guideline outranks a tier-2 product label for a dose, so NG198 leads and the label figure is recorded here.',"Oral antibiotic","100 mg once daily with food or fluid","12 weeks, reviewed at 12 weeks; a further 12 weeks only if the acne has improved but not cleared",u.iq)
B.aGf=new A.l("acute-bronchiolitis","Paracetamol",u.u,"oral.solid",u.m,"If fever",null,null,u.o)
B.aDE=new A.l("acute-lymphadenitis","Cephalexin","Mild/moderate infection: 25\u201350 mg/kg/day orally, divided every 6 or 12 h; maximum 2,000 mg/day.","oral.solid","Egyptian National Drug Formulary - antimicrobial-2023.pdf, Cephalexin monograph (chapter PDF p220)",null,"250 to 1,000 mg every 6 hours, or 500 mg every 12 hours (maximum 4 g/day)","As directed (typically 7-10 days for a straightforward skin/lymph node infection)",u.wm)
B.aEJ=new A.l("acute-pancreatitis","Paracetamol","Pancreatitis: hospital admission; paracetamol only if selected by the admitting team. Age/form-specific source regimen remains in Notes.","oral.solid","MSF Essential Drugs 2024 - paracetamol (oral): adult 1 g 3 or 4 times daily, maximum 4 g daily; child 1 month and over 15 mg/kg 3 or 4 times daily, maximum 60 mg/kg daily; child under 1 month 10 mg/kg 3 or 4 times daily, maximum 40 mg/kg daily. The 500 mg per-dose ceiling used in the weight table is MSF's own top paediatric band, one 500 mg tablet three times daily from 30 to under 50 kg.","If selected by the admitting team as a non-opioid adjunct to hospital pain treatment",u.U,"While the pain lasts; not a reason to delay admission by a single hour",u.dF)
B.aEn=new A.l("acute-vomiting-adult","Granisetron","No sourced oral child regimen; the IV oncology regimen must not be extrapolated.","oral.solid","Egyptian National Drug Formulary - Gastrointestinal Tract 2025 (granisetron monograph)",null,"1 mg twice daily or 2 mg once daily by mouth; the first dose is taken 1 hour before the emetogenic stimulus","Up to one week",u.ie)
B.aAG=new A.l("adrenal-insufficiency","Prednisone","Pediatric endocrinology: hydrocortisone replacement; no sourced child prednisone maintenance dose.","oral.solid","Adrenal Insufficiency (Addison's Disease - Maintenance) - disease-level clinical article (adrenal-insufficiency-referral-clinical.txt)","Choose one glucocorticoid replacement","Prednisone 5 mg (2.5 to 7.5 mg) orally at bedtime","long-term lifelong",u.Yx)
B.aAo=new A.l("anal-fistula","Infliximab","Pediatric gastroenterology/surgery; Crohn\u2019s licence is age 6\u201317, not a dedicated fistula regimen.","injection","Remsima 100 mg powder for concentrate for solution for infusion (infliximab) SmPC sections 4.1, 4.2, 4.3 and 4.4 (eMC product 3709)","Anti-TNF biologic for perianal fistulising Crohn's disease - hospital-initiated",'Intravenous infusion, dosed by body weight, with a three-dose induction. SmPC verbatim, for fistulising, active Crohn\'s disease: "5 mg/kg given as an intravenous infusion followed by additional 5 mg/kg infusions at 2 and 6 weeks after the first infusion." Maintenance verbatim: "Additional infusions of 5 mg/kg every 8 weeks".','Stopped after three doses if nothing has changed. SmPC verbatim: "If a patient does not respond after 3 doses, no additional treatment with infliximab should be given."',u.F9)
