B.aHH=new A.l("barretts-esophagus","Esomeprazole","Pediatric gastroenterology; no Barrett\u2019s regimen. Reflux dosing is a different indication.","oral.solid",'Egyptian National Drug Formulary - GIT medicines (git.pdf), Esomeprazole monograph, PDF page index 74 (printed p64), under "Long-term management of patients with healed esophagitis to prevent relapse". The formulary carries no Barrett\'s oesophagus indication; this is its maintenance dose for healed oesophagitis.',null,"20 mg by mouth once daily, continued long term.","Long-term/ongoing. The formulary sets no end point for relapse prevention and gives no Barrett's-specific duration.",u.Uw)
B.aHx=new A.l("blepharitis","Doxycycline","Under 8: severe/life-threatening infection or no better alternative only; specialist decision, not routine blepharitis treatment.","oral.solid",u.fw,null,"50-100 mg once daily orally for 4-6 weeks for severe posterior blepharitis / meibomian gland dysfunction","4-6 weeks",u.c)
