B.aBf=new A.l("candidiasis-of-nails","Itraconazole","Child nail disease: specialist assessment for immune disease; no sourced nail-treatment dose.","oral.solid",'SPORANOX (itraconazole) Capsules US prescribing information, DailyMed set id a4d555fa-787c-40fb-bb7d-b0d4f7318fd0, revised 7/2026, DOSAGE AND ADMINISTRATION - verbatim: "Toenails with or without fingernail involvement The recommended dose is 200 mg (2 capsules) once daily for 12 consecutive weeks." and "Fingernails only The recommended dosing regimen is 2 treatment pulses, each consisting of 200 mg (2 capsules) b.i.d. (400 mg/day) for 1 week. The pulses are separated by a 3-week period without SPORANOX." The Egyptian formulary gives the same two schedules - Egyptian National Drug Formulary 2023 - Antimicrobial (Version 1.0), itraconazole monograph (formulary page 45) - verbatim: "Onychomycosis: Note: Other agents are preferred for dermatophyte onychomycosis. Oral: Capsule or tablet: Continuous dosing: 200 mg once daily for 6 weeks or 12 weeks. Pulsed dosing: 200 mg twice daily for 1 week; repeat every 4 weeks for 2 months or 3 months".',"Oral azole for a culture-confirmed candidal nail","200 mg once daily for 12 weeks where a toenail is involved; for fingernails only, 200 mg twice daily for 1 week, repeated after 3 weeks without it","12 weeks continuous for toenails, or 2 one-week pulses for fingernails",u.ql)
