B.aDX=new A.l("immunodeficiency","Immunoglobulin","Primary humoral immunodeficiency, age \u22652 years: immunology-prescribed infusion; source replacement regimen in Notes.","injection",'GAMUNEX-C (immune globulin injection, human, 10% liquid) US prescribing information, DailyMed set id ade6b84a-e95b-0a49-3296-f56208fdf35b, section 2.1 Recommended Dosage - verbatim: "The dose of GAMUNEX-C for patients with PI is 300 mg/kg to 600 mg/kg body weight (3 mL/kg to 6 mL/kg) administered every 3 to 4 weeks." The indication comes from Immunodeficiency Disorders (Primary and Secondary) - StatPearls (NBK500027) - verbatim: "Immunoglobulin replacement therapy is the mainstay of treatment for antibody deficiencies (X-linked agammaglobulinemia, common variable immunodeficiency, hyper-IgM syndromes, and other conditions with impaired antibody production)."',"Antibody replacement (specialist-initiated)","300 mg/kg to 600 mg/kg by intravenous infusion, every 3 to 4 weeks","Lifelong in an antibody deficiency, unless a transplant cures it",u.Bw)
