B.aCJ=new A.l("malaria-uncomplicated","Primaquine","Fever-hospital specialist: review G6PD and pregnancy/lactation status before radical cure; no routine child regimen displayed.","oral.solid","Primaquine phosphate tablets, film coated (sanofi-aventis U.S. LLC) US prescribing information, Indications and Usage, Contraindications, Warnings and Dosage and Administration (DailyMed SetID 1bfbf4ae-81b8-4160-a00d-6322aadd4b59)","If confirmed P. vivax or P. ovale and G6PD result plus pregnancy/lactation status are reviewed; add to selected blood-stage treatment","Given alongside chloroquine, not instead of it. The US label dose is 1 tablet (26.3 mg, equivalent to 15 mg base) once daily for 14 days, to clear liver-stage parasites; it may be taken with or without food.",'Fourteen days, and the course is what prevents the relapse rather than what treats the attack. US label verbatim: "daily for 14 days", and the drug is "recommended only for the radical cure of vivax malaria, the prevention of relapse in vivax malaria, or following the termination of chloroquine phosphate suppressive therapy in an area where vivax malaria is endemic."',u.RG)
B.aB_=new A.l("measles","Immunoglobulin","Measles exposure: urgent product-specific IM immunoglobulin assessment within 6 days; do not give with measles vaccine. Vaccine timing changes.","injection","GAMASTAN (immune globulin (human)) injection US prescribing information, section 1 Indications and Usage and section 2 Dosage and Administration (DailyMed SetID 561f48de-2697-4a35-8233-bd1cdb73438f)","Post-exposure prophylaxis for a contact who cannot have the vaccine - intramuscular only",'0.25 mL/kg intramuscularly. US label verbatim, from its dosing table: "0.25 mL/kg" with the instruction "Administer to a susceptible person within 6 days of exposure." For an immunocompromised contact the label doubles it: "0.5 mL/kg Immediately administer (maximum dose, 15 mL) to an immunocompromised child." Route is not a choice - "For intramuscular use only." and "Do not administer intravenously." Large volumes are split: "Divide and inject doses greater than 10 mL into several muscle sites to reduce local pain and discomfort."','One dose, tied to the exposure rather than to symptoms. The label\'s window is six days from contact, and an immunocompromised child is dosed "Immediately".',u.kl)
