B.aFU=new A.l("routine-immunisation-catch-up","Oral poliomyelitis vaccine","Oral polio: 2 drops on tongue per scheduled visit; \u22654 weeks between doses. Vomiting/diarrhoea: extra dose after recovery; follow Egyptian schedule.","oral.liquid",'MSF Essential Drugs 2024 (ORAL POLIOMYELITIS VACCINE (OPV) monograph, p536) - verbatim: "One dose = 2 drops (approximately 0.1 ml)" and, on whose schedule governs, same monograph, verbatim: "For the vaccination schedule, follow national recommendations."; that national schedule is Egypt\'s own, from WHO/UNICEF national immunisation schedule for Egypt, 2025 (WHO Immunization Data portal, WIISE AD_SCHEDULES, data/reference/library/who-egypt-immunisation-schedule-2025.txt), which places OPV rounds 1 to 7 at birth and at 2, 4, 6, 9, 12 and 18 months; the Ministry of Health and Population timetable places the zero dose in the first month instead, and that difference is unresolved.',"Polio - oral drops","One dose = 2 drops (approximately 0.1 mL) placed on the tongue from the dropper","Seven doses in Egypt: at birth and at 2, 4, 6, 9, 12 and 18 months",u.J8)
B.aEO=new A.l("routine-immunisation-catch-up","Inactivated poliomyelitis vaccine","IPV: 0.5 mL/dose; follow Egyptian schedule and selected product\u2019s route. Do not substitute fractional intradermal regimen.","injection",'MSF Essential Drugs 2024 (INACTIVATED POLIOMYELITIS VACCINE (IPV) monograph, p534) - verbatim: "IPV only schedule Child: 3 doses of 0.5 ml approximately 4 weeks apart, at 6, 10 and 14 weeks of age and a booster dose at least 6 months after the 3 dose" - the ages inside that line are MSF\'s own schedule and the figure taken from it is the 0.5 mL. On whose schedule governs, same monograph, verbatim: "Certain countries have vaccination schedules for children and adults that use only the injectable vaccine and include booster doses: follow national recommendations."; the ages here are Egypt\'s own, from WHO/UNICEF national immunisation schedule for Egypt, 2025 (WHO Immunization Data portal, WIISE AD_SCHEDULES, data/reference/library/who-egypt-immunisation-schedule-2025.txt), which places IPV rounds 1, 2 and 3 at 2, 4 and 6 months.',"Polio - injected","0.5 mL as a single dose, intramuscularly into the anterolateral thigh under 2 years of age, or by deep subcutaneous injection into the deltoid from 2 years and in adults","Three doses in Egypt, at 2, 4 and 6 months",u.Ul)
B.aBL=new A.l("routine-immunisation-catch-up","Measles, mumps and rubella vaccine","Priorix: 0.5 mL/dose, licensed from 9 months. Vaccinated in infancy: second dose in second year, \u22654 weeks later; follow Egyptian schedule.","injection",'Priorix powder and solvent for solution for injection in a pre-filled syringe - UK Summary of Product Characteristics, electronic Medicines Compendium product 1159, section 4.2 - verbatim: "The dose is 0.5 ml. A second dose should be given according to official recommendations." Corroborated for a measles-containing vaccine by MSF Essential Drugs 2024 (MEASLES VACCINE monograph, p522) - verbatim: "Child between 9 and 12 months: one dose of 0.5 ml."; the ages are Egypt\'s own, from WHO/UNICEF national immunisation schedule for Egypt, 2025 (WHO Immunization Data portal, WIISE AD_SCHEDULES, data/reference/library/who-egypt-immunisation-schedule-2025.txt), which places MMR round 1 at 12 months and round 2 at 18 months.',"Measles, mumps and rubella","0.5 mL, subcutaneously, or intramuscularly into the deltoid region or the anterolateral thigh","Two doses in Egypt, at 12 months and at 18 months",u.JL)
