B.a0B={"100-200 mcg (1-2 puffs of 100 mcg/puff) as needed for acute symptom relief":0,"0.5 mg (0.5 mL of 1:1000 / 1 mg/mL solution) INTRAMUSCULARLY into mid-outer thigh. Repeat every 5 minutes PRN if no improvement.":1,"20 mg twice daily as the PPI component - of the quadruple regimen on line 1, and of the triple regimen on line 2":2,"20 mg twice daily as the PPI component of the triple regimen - the same drug and dose as in regimen A":3,"Apply 5% cream over the whole body from the neck down, including neck, palms and soles, and wash off after 8-14 hours; repeat 7-14 days after the first treatment. Up to 30 g (one 30 g tube) per application":4,"200 micrograms/kg orally with food; repeat 14 days after the first dose.":5,"Apply the 25% lotion at night after bathing, over the whole body from the neck down; let it dry, apply a second coat, and wash it off the next morning. It may be repeated after 24 hours.":6,"Plan A (no dehydration): Drink as much ORS as desired after each loose stool. If Plan B is selected (some dehydration): give 75 mL/kg ORS over the first 4 hours in a health facility under observation, then reassess.":7,"Three capsules four times a day, after meals and at bedtime. Each capsule contains bismuth subcitrate potassium 140 mg, metronidazole 125 mg and tetracycline hydrochloride 125 mg. Give with omeprazole 20 mg twice daily.":8,'A three-day course with a double first dose. SmPC verbatim: "Acute uncomplicated cystitis: 72 hour course of 2 tablets immediately followed by 1 tablet 3 times daily to a total of 10 tablets." On 200 mg tablets that is 400 mg once, then 200 mg three times a day. For a bacteriuria that keeps returning the SmPC gives a heavier regimen: "Chronic or recurrent bacteriuria: 2 tablets three to four times daily."':9}
B.eE=new A.aW(B.a0B,["100\u2013200 mcg (1\u20132 puffs of 100 mcg/puff) as needed for acute relief.","0.5 mg (0.5 mL of 1 mg/mL [1:1000]) IM into mid-outer thigh; repeat every 5 min if no improvement.","Omeprazole 20 mg twice daily with either regimen.","Omeprazole 20 mg twice daily with triple therapy.","5% cream: apply neck down, including neck, palms and soles. Wash off after 8\u201314 h; repeat 7\u201314 days after first application. Max 30 g/application.","200 micrograms/kg orally with food; repeat after 14 days.","25% lotion: after bathing at night, apply whole body neck-down. Let dry, apply a second coat; wash off next morning. May repeat after 24 h.","Plan A (no dehydration): ORS as desired after each loose stool.\nPlan B (some dehydration): 75 mL/kg over 4 h in a health facility under observation; reassess.","3 capsules four times daily, after meals and at bedtime.\nEach capsule: bismuth subcitrate potassium 140 mg + metronidazole 125 mg + tetracycline hydrochloride 125 mg.\nWith omeprazole 20 mg twice daily.","200 mg tablets: 400 mg once, then 200 mg three times daily.\n72-hour course; total 10 tablets.\nRecurrent bacteriuria: separate 400 mg 3\u20134 times daily regimen."],t.li)
