B.awJ=new A.b2(u.k7,!0)
B.ax1=new A.b2(u.Hp,!0)
B.awr=new A.b2("Assess for associated clavicle fracture, sternoclavicular injury or neurovascular injury before calling it a sprain.",!0)
B.axi=new A.b2("Treating-service regimen: refer before starting.",!0)
B.aw8=new A.b2("Max 4 g/24 h (adult); 60 mg/kg/24 h (child). Overdose can cause severe liver injury; take extra care in children and older adults.",!0)
B.axg=new A.b2("MSF reassurance on pregnancy, breastfeeding and aspirin allergy.",!1)
B.awz=new A.b2("Purulent sputum alone does not establish bacterial infection or justify antibiotics.",!0)
B.awb=new A.b2("Max 5 consecutive days.",!0)
B.ax_=new A.b2("Max 8 sprays/24 h (adults); 4 sprays/24 h (children).",!0)
B.axf=new A.b2("Contraindicated: MAO inhibitors (past 2 weeks), narrow-angle glaucoma, acute coronary disease or cardiac asthma, rhinitis sicca, post-transsphenoidal hypophysectomy.",!0)
B.aw9=new A.b2("Caution: coronary heart disease, hypertension, hyperthyroidism, diabetes; prostatic enlargement with difficulty urinating.",!0)
B.awy=new A.b2("Max 4 g/day (adults); 60 mg/kg/day (children).",!0)
B.awD=new A.b2("Frequency from practice; label gives no spray count or schedule.",!0)
B.awu=new A.b2("Blood-stained sputum: urgent work-up.",!0)
B.awV=new A.b2("Large-volume purulent sputum: assess bronchiectasis; refer.",!0)
B.awt=new A.b2("Persistent symptoms + weight loss/night sweats: TB work-up before/alongside antibiotics.",!0)
B.awn=new A.b2("Penicillin allergy: avoid.",!0)
B.ax9=new A.b2("Severe renal impairment: reduce dose.",!0)
B.aw3=new A.b2("Glandular fever: rash risk.",!0)
B.awK=new A.b2("Suspected diphtheria or deep-space abscess: immediate intervention.",!0)
B.axh=new A.b2("Peritonsillar abscess/suppurative complication: hospital care; drainage/IV treatment.",!0)
B.awH=new A.b2("Honey: never under 1 year (infant botulism risk). Source gives no quantity, frequency or duration.",!0)
B.awB=new A.b2("Count all paracetamol toward the daily maximum.",!0)
B.aw6=new A.b2("Severe acute malnutrition: 10 mg/kg/dose; max 3 doses/24 h.",!0)
B.awZ=new A.b2("Dengue with warning signs: 10 mg/kg/dose, 3-4 times daily.",!0)
B.awG=new A.b2("Hepatic impairment: caution.",!0)
B.ax7=new A.b2("Uncomplicated viral cold/acute bronchitis: no routine antibiotics or antivirals.",!0)
B.aw7=new A.b2("Assess for GAS pharyngitis, severe acute otitis media, or sinusitis lasting over 10 days/worsening after initial improvement; these need a different pathway.",!0)
B.aw1=new A.b2("Avoid OTC cough/cold preparations in children under 12; they have no proven benefit and overdoses can be fatal. Sources give different lower age cut-offs.",!0)
B.aww=new A.b2("Under 6 years: cough/cold medicines carry risk; antihistamine/decongestant overdose can be fatal.",!0)
B.awR=new A.b2("Codeine: do not use in children.",!0)
B.awc=new A.b2("Dextromethorphan: no proven benefit in children. Formulary permits syrup from 6 years and contraindicates tablets below 12; clinical sources disagree. Not offered here.",!0)
B.ax5=new A.b2("Benzonatate: safety/effectiveness unestablished; not advised under 10 years.",!0)
B.aw_=new A.b2("Assess urgently: abnormal observations, hypoxia/blue lips, altered consciousness, vomiting, recurrent pneumonia, immunocompromise, dysphagia or poor intake.",!0)
B.ax8=new A.b2("Sudden cough/choking: urgently assess for an inhaled foreign body.",!0)
B.avZ=new A.b2("Suspected pneumonia: chest X-ray and full blood count; CRP selectively. CRP over 30 mg/L supports pneumonia in the right clinical context. Uncomplicated cold, acute bronchitis, acute rhinosinusitis or allergic rhinitis: no routine tests without complication signs.",!0)
B.awP=new A.b2("Under 2 years + wheeze/crackles, tachypnoea or chest indrawing: assess bronchiolitis.",!0)
B.axd=new A.b2("Wet cough for 4 weeks or more: assess protracted bacterial bronchitis; do not start its antibiotic course at the first acute-cough visit.",!0)
B.awL=new A.b2("Aspirin allergy: paracetamol is a preferred option.",!1)
B.awE=new A.b2("High fever, pharyngitis/tonsillitis, otitis, cervical adenopathy, wheeze, productive cough or dyspnoea: assess for complications or another diagnosis.",!0)
B.awX=new A.b2("Severe acute otitis media, sinusitis over 10 days or worsening after initial improvement: assess for antibiotics. Otherwise no routine antibiotics.",!0)
B.awk=new A.b2("Never use SABA alone; prescribe an ICS with it, at every age.",!0)
B.awY=new A.b2("Not for acute relief.",!0)
B.aw4=new A.b2("Give IM adrenaline immediately for airway, breathing or circulation compromise.",!0)
B.axa=new A.b2("IV adrenaline: specialist setting and experienced clinician only. Persistent breathing/circulation problems after 2 IM doses: seek expert help.",!0)
B.awU=new A.b2("Lie flat, legs raised; sit up if breathlessness dominates. Do not stand or walk abruptly.",!0)
B.axb=new A.b2("Call resuscitation team/ambulance; arrange emergency assessment.",!0)
B.awS=new A.b2("Steroids: not for routine anaphylaxis treatment.",!0)
B.awq=new A.b2("Never delay adrenaline, fluids or adrenaline infusion for hydrocortisone.",!0)
B.aw2=new A.b2("Never prioritise corticosteroids over adrenaline.",!0)
B.awF=new A.b2("Risk-stratify hospital observation; a senior clinician decides further treatment and duration.",!0)
B.ax3=new A.b2("14 days yields higher eradication than 7 days.",!1)
B.awh=new A.b2("Continue omeprazole 20 mg twice daily with either regimen.",!0)
B.ax2=new A.b2("Tetracycline binds fetal bone/teeth: contraindicated in pregnancy/breastfeeding; defer eradication or refer.",!0)
B.awv=new A.b2("First-line avoids clarithromycin. Guidelines use a 15% local resistance cutoff for empirical triple therapy; Egypt\u2019s rate is undocumented.",!0)
B.awm=new A.b2("Avoid alcohol with metronidazole; take tetracycline with a full glass of water.",!0)
B.ax4=new A.b2("BISPYLLER/TRIGASTCARE: 650\u2013800 EGP. Cheaper Egyptian options exist, but resistance makes them non-preferred first-line.",!1)
B.awM=new A.b2("Use omeprazole with either regimen, not both; the regimens are alternatives.",!0)
B.awd=new A.b2("Use only if clarithromycin susceptibility is confirmed or local resistance is <15%; Egypt\u2019s rate is undocumented.",!0)
